Package: com.andi.claude-code-native
Name: Claude Code (native)
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: andi <tafilajandi@gmail.com>
Author: Anthropic (upstream) / iOS port by andi
Section: Development
Priority: optional
Depends: zsh, python3, ldid, curl, tar, gzip, coreutils, uikittools, firmware (>= 15.0)
Icon: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/@REPO@/main/assets/icon.png
Native-Depiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.json
SileoDepiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.json
Tag: role::developer
Description: Anthropic's Claude Code CLI, native build, patched for iOS
 Packages Claude Code @CC_VERSION@.
 .
 The official darwin-arm64 Claude Code executable (Bun-compiled) made to run on
 jailbroken iOS. Upstream stopped shipping a JavaScript cli.js after 2.1.112, so
 this packages the native binary instead.
 .
 Sign in with `claude auth login` or /login, as on a Mac. Claude Code reaches
 the keychain by shelling out to macOS's `security`, and opens links with
 `open`; iOS has neither, so this package ships a stand-in for each -- the
 keychain one backed by the real iOS keychain, the other by uiopen. Without the
 first, a sign-in used to be discarded silently the moment it succeeded.
 .
 `claude-login` is still there for a device whose keychain refuses (the install
 probes it and says so), and for anyone already using it: while its credential
 exists it owns sign-in, keeps the token refreshed, and the native commands
 defer to it. `claude-login --logout` removes every copy.
 .
 Updates come from this repository, so Claude Code's own updater is off and its
 update notices with it. The wrapper checks the repository for a newer package
 instead, in the background and at most once a day; CCIOS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1
 turns that off.
 .
 The credential's master copy is stored in the iOS keychain (this-device-only,
 via the ccauth-keychain helper), not as a plain-text file: the long-lived
 refresh token never touches the file system, and the keychain item is
 destroyed by "Erase All Content and Settings" and excluded from backups.
 A jailbroken device still has no security boundary for anything running as
 root -- run `claude-login --logout` before passing the device on.
 .
 The binary itself is NOT redistributed here. On install this package downloads
 the official tarball straight from the npm registry, verifies its SHA-256, and
 patches it on device: Mach-O platform to iOS, a small shim linked in for the
 four libSystem symbols iOS lacks, and the macOS framework dlopen paths
 rewritten. Takes a few seconds.
 .
 The shim also makes JSC's JIT work, which is not optional: iOS has no MAP_JIT
 and refuses to execute a writable page, and without JIT JavaScriptCore disables
 SharedArrayBuffer, which Claude Code needs at startup. The shim keeps each page
 of the JIT pool writable or executable and repairs the fault when a thread
 needs the other, one page at a time, so worker threads are safe.
 .
 Needs an A12 chip or newer. A12-class devices (iPhone XS/XR, 2018 iPad Pro,
 iPad Air 3, iPad mini 5, iPad 8th gen) are experimental: the official build
 uses a few CPU instructions they lack, which the shim emulates, and some
 errors can occur. On an older chip the install stops and says why.
